Source: homelab-postfix
Section: mail
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/permittivity2/homelab

Package: homelab-postfix
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, postfix, postfix-pgsql, homelab-dovecot (>= 0.1.2), adduser, postgresql-client
Description: SMTP submission/relay wired to the homelab-* shared identity
 Wires Postfix to the shared `homelab` Postgres database for recipient
 validation only -- a narrow, column-scoped cross-schema grant (email/
 active, no password_hash at all -- see
 script/homelab-postfix-bootstrap-role) backing a virtual_mailbox_maps
 pgsql lookup that decides accept/reject at RCPT TO time. SASL
 authentication for the submission service is delegated entirely to
 Dovecot's own passdb over a unix socket (smtpd_sasl_type = dovecot) --
 Postfix never queries Postgres for credentials itself. One Argon2id
 password in api.users backs both, but each service holds its own
 narrowly-scoped secret: the unified cross-feature identity design
 described in CLAUDE.md. Accepted mail is handed to homelab-dovecot over
 LMTP (127.0.0.1:24).
 .
 Like homelab-dovecot, this package owns no schema/tables of its own and
 therefore has no migrate role, unlike the standard split runtime/
 migrate Postgres role pattern most other homelab-* features use --
 an intentional, documented exception (see README.md), not an oversight.
 .
 Depends on homelab-dovecot as a hard runtime requirement, not just a
 recommendation: SASL authentication and all mail delivery both fail
 without it (the SASL socket and the LMTP listener it delivers to are
 both provided by homelab-dovecot).
